        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Intent Classifier"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772560572194"
          },
          "code": "INTENT_CLASSIFIER",
          "id": "1772560230951",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772560230952_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intent classifier. Classify the user message as exactly one intent.\n\nUser message: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n- **create**: The user wants to create/add/implement/define/write/set up a rule now, and the request is either generic or a supported rule type.\n- **similarity**: The user wants to check whether a similar/existing rule already exists, compare against existing rules, or run a similarity/duplication check.\n- **generic**: The user is asking for instructions/explanations/capabilities, or is requesting creation of an unsupported rule type.\n\n### Supported create rule types\n- Constrain\n- Recommendation\n- Hiding\n- Message (optional)\n\n### Key distinction\n- If the user asks **to do the action now** -> classify as **create** or **similarity**.\n- If the user asks **how to do it / what it means / guidance** -> classify as **generic**, even if words like “create” or “similarity” appear.\n\n### Unsupported type handling (critical)\nIf the user asks to create/add/define/implement/set up a **specific rule type** that is not in the supported list above, classify as **generic**.\n\nTreat these as unsupported (including close variants):\n- BOM rule\n- BOM mapping rule\n- Pricing rule\n- Validation rule\n- Recommended item rule (different from Recommendation rule)\n\nExamples that must be **generic**:\n- “Create a BOM rule.”\n- “Create a BOM Mapping Rule.”\n- “Add a BOM mapping rule for part numbers.”\n- “Create a Pricing Rule.”\n- “Create a Validation Rule.”\n- “Create a Recommended Item Rule.”\n\n### Decision rules (priority order)\n1) **Generic instructional/capabilities queries override keywords**  \nIf the message is about instructions or learning, classify as **generic**.  \nExamples:\n- “how do I…”, “how to…”, “can you explain…”, “what is…”, “what can you do…”, “help me…”, “examples of…”, “documentation…”, “tutorial…”, “when should I…”\n\n2) **Unsupported specific rule type requests**  \nIf creation is requested for a specific unsupported type, classify as **generic**.\n\n3) **Similarity intent**  \nClassify as **similarity** if the user asks to check existence/similarity.  \nExamples:\n- “is there already a rule…”\n- “do we have a rule for…”\n- “does something similar exist…”\n- “find similar rules…”\n- “compare against existing rules…”\n- “run a similarity check…”\n\n4) **Create intent**  \nClassify as **create** if the user requests rule creation now and does not specify an unsupported type.  \nExamples:\n- “create/add/write/define/implement/set up a rule that…”\n- “make a rule to…”\n- “new rule: …”\n- rule-spec format: “when/if [condition] then [action]”\n\n5) **Fallback**  \nAnything else -> **generic**.\n\n### Output format\nReturn ONLY valid JSON in exactly one of these forms:\n{\"intent\":\"create\"}\n{\"intent\":\"similarity\"}\n{\"intent\":\"generic\"}\n\n---\n\n## Quick examples\n\n**generic**\n- “How to create a rule?”\n- “How do I perform a similarity check?”\n- “What can you do?”\n- “What kinds of rules can be created?”\n- “Can you explain what a similarity check means?”\n- “Create a BOM rule.”\n- “Create a BOM Mapping Rule.”\n- “Create a Pricing Rule.”\n- “Create a Validation Rule.”\n- “Create a Recommended Item Rule.”\n\n**create**\n- “Create a rule that blocks submissions after 5pm.”\n- “Add a rule: if country=DE then require VAT ID.”\n- “Set up a constraint: when amount > 10k, require approval.”\n- “When vcolor is black, interior must be white.”\n\n**similarity**\n- “Do we already have a rule for VAT validation?”\n- “Find a similar rule to: if amount > 10k require approval.”\n- “Compare this rule to existing ones and tell me if it duplicates anything.”"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"intent\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM",
