        {
          "id": "1775855768839",
          "code": "ACTION_BUILDER_LLM",
          "type": "LLM",
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Action Builder LLM"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 6859.5,
            "y": 7514
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775856335723"
          },
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775855768839_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a product-configuration action builder.\n\nINPUTS\n1) User Rule Description (string):\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n\n2) Model Attributes & MenuItems (JSON):\n{{$context.$variables.attributes}}\n\nGOAL\nExtract only the action logic and return a normalized actions array:\n\n[\n  {\n    \"attribute\": <string|null>,\n    \"values\": [<string>, ...]\n  }\n]\n\nDo not return any wrapper object. Do not return conditions. JSON array only.\n\nACTION VS CONDITION SPLIT (STRICT)\n- Ignore condition clauses introduced by words like: if, when, where, unless, given.\n- Keep only outcome/action clauses.\n- Treat a clause as action if it contains intent words such as:\n  should, must, set, force, constrain, allow, disallow, recommend, hide, show, display, message\n\nExample:\nInput: \"Check for similar rules where the color is black, the interior should be white\"\nOutput action should be interior=white only.\n\nEXTRACTION RULES\n1) Attribute\n- \"attribute\" must be one of the provided attribute variable names.\n- Do not invent attribute names.\n- If no valid attribute can be identified for an action clause, skip that clause.\n\n2) Values\n- \"values\" must always be an array.\n- For hide/show-style actions with no explicit value, use [].\n- For set/recommend/constrain-style actions, extract explicit values from text.\n- For menu attributes, map to the closest valid menu item from metadata.\n- Preserve exact metadata casing for selected values.\n- If value cannot be confidently resolved, keep the action with values [].\n\n3) Message-like action\n- If action is only a user-facing message and no attribute target exists:\n  {\n    \"attribute\": null,\n    \"values\": [\"<message text>\"]\n  }\n- Never invent message text.\n\n4) Dedup\n- Deduplicate identical {attribute, values} entries.\n\n5) Empty result\n- If no action can be extracted, return [].\n\nOUTPUT FORMAT\nReturn valid JSON only (no markdown, no commentary), for example:\n[\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"vInterior\",\n    \"values\": [\n      \"black\"\n    ]\n  }\n]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Condition Builder LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775012540050"
          },
          "code": "CONDITION_BUILDER_LLM",
          "id": "1775011915866",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775011915866_systemPrompt",
              "name": "systemPrompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": ""
            },
            {
              "id": "1775011915866_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a product-configuration condition builder.\n\nINPUTS\n1. User Rule Description (string):\n{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n2. Model Attributes & MenuItems (JSON):\n{{$context.$variables.attributes}}\n\nTASK\nExtract only predicate logic (the \"if/when\" part). Ignore all outcomes/actions.\n\nSTRICT SPLIT RULE\nTreat text as ACTION (not condition) if it contains intent words such as:\n- should, must, set, make, force, constrain, allow, recommend, hide, show, display, message\nExample:\n\"If color is black, interior should be white\"\n- Condition: color = black\n- Action: interior = white (do NOT include this in conditions)\n\nIf no predicates exist, return exactly this sentinel:\n[\n  {\n    \"criteria\": {\n      \"criteriaType\": \"Attribute\",\n      \"attribute\": \"_alwaysTrue\"\n    },\n    \"operator\": \"EqualTo\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"valueType\": \"Static\",\n      \"values\": [\n        \"true\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nOUTPUT\nReturn only a JSON array of condition objects (no wrapper, no markdown, no commentary).\n\nREQUIRED SHAPE\n[\n  {\n    \"criteria\": {\n      \"criteriaType\": \"Attribute\",\n      \"attribute\": <string>\n    },\n    \"operator\": <string>,\n    \"value\": {\n      \"valueType\": \"Static\",\n      \"values\": [\n        <string>,\n        ...\n      ],\n      \"rangeOperator\": <string, optional>,\n      \"rangeValue\": [\n        <string>,\n        ...\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nDETAILED RULES\nA. Condition Items\n- criteria.criteriaType is always \"Attribute\".\n- criteria.attribute must be one of provided attribute variable names; do not invent names.\n- operator must be valid for the attribute inputTypeCode:\n  - SingleSelectMenu: EqualTo, NotEqualTo\n  - MultiSelectMenu: EqualTo, NotEqualTo, Contains, NotContains\n  - TextField + dataType \"Text\": EqualTo, NotEqualTo, Contains, NotContains, StartsWith, NotStartsWith, EndsWith, NotEndsWith\n  - TextField + dataType \"Integer\"/\"Float\": LessThan, LessThanEqualTo, EqualTo, NotEqualTo, GreaterThan, GreaterThanEqualTo, Between\n  - Date: EqualTo, NotEqualTo, Before, OnOrBefore, After, OnOrAfter, Between\n  - Currency: LessThan, LessThanEqualTo, EqualTo, NotEqualTo, GreaterThan, GreaterThanEqualTo, Between\n  - Boolean: EqualTo\n- For Between: lower bound in value.values, upper bound in value.rangeValue, and set value.rangeOperator.\n- For non-Between: omit rangeOperator and rangeValue.\n\nB. Values\n- Use exact casing from metadata.\n- SingleSelectMenu and MultiSelectMenu may contain multiple values.\n- All other input types must contain exactly one value.\n- Do not fabricate values not in metadata.\n- If any required predicate value cannot be resolved, return the sentinel.\n\nC. General\n- Do not add conditionExpression, conditionType, index, level, or wrapper objects.\n- Do not emit actions/recommendations/messages.\n- Preserve original string casing; no extra whitespace padding.\n\nEXAMPLES\nInput: \"If color is black, interior should be white\"\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"criteria\": {\n      \"criteriaType\": \"Attribute\",\n      \"attribute\": \"vColor\"\n    },\n    \"operator\": \"EqualTo\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"valueType\": \"Static\",\n      \"values\": [\n        \"black\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]\n\nInput: \"Interior should be white\"\nOutput:\n[\n  {\n    \"criteria\": {\n      \"criteriaType\": \"Attribute\",\n      \"attribute\": \"_alwaysTrue\"\n    },\n    \"operator\": \"EqualTo\",\n    \"value\": {\n      \"valueType\": \"Static\",\n      \"values\": [\n        \"true\"\n      ]\n    }\n  }\n]"
            }
          ],
